Z||000000||mshill||04-19-2000||02:27 PM||||Yesterday I took my 86SE V6 into the Big-O Tires here in Rocklin, CA for a 4 wheel alignment and balance.  I got a call this <BR>morning from the guy there that said he had some kind of problem with the machine. He said "There's something magnetic or electrical in the car that interfered with the analysis so no adjustments could be made."  He claimed that it even existed with the car turned off and the key out of the ignition.  Of course, he didn't charge me for the alignment, but the wheel balancing did n't seem to correct the shimmy in the front end that I didn't have with my stock wheels.<P>Has anyone had this kind of a problem getting their car aligned?  Do you think that he was telling me the truth, or just didn't want to deal with the front end of the car?<P>||||reg||9
